</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Images</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attackers may manipulate either individual images embedded in a webpage or full webpage screenshots in order to influence the downstream behavior of web agents. We therefore construct our image dataset explicitly along these two dimensions, forming a collection of 2,022 malicious and 948 benign images.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:66%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Statistics of our collected images across two categories. For each category, we report malicious and benign samples.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T3.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:224.3pt;height:27.8pt;vertical-align:-12.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-139.8pt,17.3pt) scale(0.445096076607487,0.445096076607487) ;">
